# Wallpaper generation
# Custom module: modules/theme/wallpaper.nix (flake.nixosModules.wallpaper)
# Blend file + renderer: modules/theme/wallpaper.blend, render-wallpaper.py

Customizable colors (all hex, no leading #)
    var.wallpaperColors        list of stops fed into the gradient ramp,
                                 evenly spaced left to right (duplicate an
                                 entry for a wider flat band). Default:
                                 [ c.black2 c.dred c.dred c.black2 c.dcyan
                                   c.dcyan c.black2 ]
    var.wallpaperBackgroundColor  Material.001's Principled BSDF Base
                                 Color -- the flat backing material behind
                                 the ramp (visible via the Wireframe
                                 modifier's line/grid geometry, ~7% of
                                 rendered faces). Default: c.black
    var.wallpaperWorldColor    the World's Background shader color.
                                 Default: c.black2
    All three feed render-wallpaper.py as WALLPAPER_COLORS / WALLPAPER_BG /
    WALLPAPER_WORLD. Their defaults are hoisted into a shared
    defaultColors/defaultBg/defaultWorld let-binding in wallpaper.nix, also
    used by the standalone CLI below, so the two can't drift apart.

Standalone render CLI (for devices with no var.monitors entry -- phones,
tablets, etc, or anything not NixOS)
    nix run .#render-wallpaper -- [--width W --height H]
      [--colors c1,c2,...] [--bg HEX] [--world HEX] [--out PATH]
      [--samples N]
        --width/--height   must be given together; omit both to keep
                            whatever resolution is saved in wallpaper.blend
                            (currently 7680x4320)
        --colors/--bg/--world   default to the same theme values
                            wallpaperColors/wallpaperBackgroundColor/
                            wallpaperWorldColor default to above
        --out               defaults to ./wallpaper-render.png
        --samples           defaults to 64
    Example: nix run .#render-wallpaper -- --width 1170 --height 2532
      --out ~/phone.png
    Then copy the PNG over however suits the device (adb push, syncthing,
    airdrop...). Defined as packages.<system>.render-wallpaper in
    wallpaper.nix's perSystem block.
